 (state count full)←StormRule(state signature now ceiling resetAfter);keep;ind
⍝ Applies the storm guard's rules to one crash. Changes nothing on disk.\\
⍝ `state` is what `NewStormState` and `ReadStormFile` return, `now` the time of the crash in seconds (UTC),
⍝ `ceiling` and `resetAfter` are the parameters `stormCeiling` and `stormResetAfter`.\\
⍝ Returns the updated `state`, the number of occurrences of `signature`, and a Boolean that is 1
⍝ when the crash gets the full treatment, which requires both:
⍝ * the count is at least twice the count at which the signature last got the full treatment
⍝ * fewer than `ceiling` crashes got the full treatment within the last hour\\
⍝ A signature that has not occurred for `resetAfter` hours starts afresh.
 keep←(now-state.lasts)<resetAfter×3600
 state.(signatures counts lastFulls firsts lasts)←keep∘/¨state.(signatures counts lastFulls firsts lasts)
 state.fulls←((now-state.fulls)<3600)/state.fulls
 ind←state.signatures⍳⊂signature
 :If ind>≢state.signatures
     state.signatures,←⊂signature
     state.counts,←0
     state.lastFulls,←0
     state.firsts,←now
     state.lasts,←now
 :EndIf
 state.counts[ind]+←1
 state.lasts[ind]←now
 count←ind⊃state.counts
 full←(count≥2×ind⊃state.lastFulls)∧ceiling>≢state.fulls
 :If full
     state.lastFulls[ind]←count
     state.fulls,←now
 :EndIf
